{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Honor your father.</b> And it is written 'Honor HaShem from your wealth'; it is written 'Your father and your mother you shall revere,' and it is written 'HaShem your Elohim you shall revere.' It is written 'One who curses his father and his mother shall surely be put to death,' and it is written 'One who curses his Elohim shall bear his sin.' To teach that the Holy One, blessed be He, compared their matter to His matter. But it is impossible to say 'striking upward' (i.e., that honoring parents is fully equivalent to honoring Him). And likewise by right, all three of them are partners in him." "<b>Which HaShem your Elohim has given you.</b> Turnus Rufus the wicked asked Rabbi Akiva: why is the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, mentioned in the first five commandments but not mentioned in the last five commandments? Rabbi Akiva went to the palace of Turnus Rufus and showed him his spear. He went back and walked to his triclinium and showed him there his shield. He went back and walked to his writing-room and showed him there his armor and his weapons. He then brought him to his lavatory. He said to him: why did you not place your weapons here? He said to him: because it is disgraceful for me to leave them in a place of filth. Rabbi Akiva said to him: so too in the first commandments there is only a way of honor, and therefore the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, was written there; but in the last five, which speak of murder, adultery, theft, false testimony, and coveting, He did not wish to mention His name in them. Another interpretation: the first five commandments — one who transgresses them sins only against Heaven, therefore He mentioned His name in all of them, since they are established for His name; but the last five are only between people, therefore He did not bother to mention His name in them. [<b>That your days may be long.</b> Thus if you do not honor him, they will be shortened.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:06.477566988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}